            "review_title": "Review at Tan Lap Restaurant",
            "review_text": "David M\nCorona, California46 contributions\n0\nLocal but bad\nJul 2022\nVisiting family in Vietnam, stay at hotel down the street from this place. Wanted to go somewhere local to have a drink with family. Saw good selectionof liquors behind bar, so we went in. Sat down on hard stools, checked out menus, one for food and one for drinks. They had a selection of beers, some wines by the bottle and some cheap house wine by the glass. Family ordered a pork dish, they ordered beer and avacado smoothies for my wife and her sister. They do not drink. I checked out menu for mix drinks since I do not drink beer and the local wine is not that great. Asked waiter about a mix drink with the alcohol behind bar, he said, that is for show, they do not serve mixed drinks. I ordered a mojito, per the menu. Food came, got 10 pieces for triangle cut pork, cold and tasted like spam. Drinks came, wife did not like smoothie, my mojito came later, no rum, just 7 up, with cut limes and mint. They charge me a mix drink price for 7 up, not happy. We stayed because family wanted a few beers and I was paying, but food was bad and no mix drinks, waste of my time and money. The wines by the bottle were imported, one bottle from each region of the world, starting at almost 1 mil dong, or 50 bucks US, making a glass of wine at $12 a glass. All names of wineries I never heard of. Not even the US bottle. Had I had time to read a review, would of been a big pass.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten July 20, 2022",
