            "review_title": "Review at Tan Lap Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Jess F\n4 contributions\n0\nGood food, awful service\nMar 2019 • Solo\nVisited when it was quiet, just after midday. Said I was in for drink and a snack but it took a while and several requests to be given a food menu. I ordered coffee and spring rolls, the spring rolls came but the coffee didn’t, though I asked for it several times. Staff were joking with each other and shouting across the restaurant to each other- which is fine if you’ve not got any customers to see to but not when people are waiting! Some other customers near me weren’t given the right change and staff weren’t very receptive when this was pointed out. One older staff member, possibly a manager, began smoking inside which wasn’t very nice. As I was late for a trip I asked for them to not bring the coffee but was ignored by all but one girl who was clearly trying to do her job. Coffee never came anyway. I asked for the bill several times, again only one girl took any notice. Sadly she had to go next door to get anything which was really inconvinient for everyone. A large group of friends of the staff were getting all the attention. Left what I guessed was correct money but no way of knowing as the bill didn’t arrive! A real shame as the food was good and one staff member was trying to help, but a really bad experience overall.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 25, 2019",
